 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased
+
+#### 🐞 Fixes
+
+- Fixed an issue where `SIGHUP` (for example, closing the terminal) immediately killed moon without
+  shutting down running tasks, leaving their processes orphaned. Running tasks now receive `SIGHUP`
+  and moon exits 129, like it does for `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM`.
+  - On Windows, closing the console window is now also treated as a hangup, so the run is reported
+    as terminated (exit 129) instead of aborted (exit 131).
+
 ## 2.6.2
 
 #### 🐞 Fixes
